From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] bluray: report the normal time of the current clip

Without DEMUX_GET_NORMAL_TIME the player clock counts in raw clip
timestamps, which start at 600 s or anywhere, while DEMUX_GET_TIME answers
with libbluray's read position, half a second ahead of the picture: the
time a player shows jumped between the two. Report the timestamp at which
the playlist's media time is zero, as the TS demuxer does with its first
PCR.
---
 modules/access/bluray.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/access/bluray.c b/modules/access/bluray.c
index abe0efb..3364215 100644
--- a/modules/access/bluray.c
+++ b/modules/access/bluray.c
@@ -2478,6 +2478,19 @@ static int blurayControl(demux_t *p_demux, int query, va_list args)
         return VLC_SUCCESS;
     }
 
+    case DEMUX_GET_NORMAL_TIME:
+    {
+        /* The timestamp media time 0 of the playlist corresponds to: without
+         * it the player clock counts in raw clip timestamps, which start at
+         * 600 s or anywhere, and the time shown jumps between the two. */
+        const BLURAY_CLIP_INFO *clip = p_sys->p_clip_info;
+        if(clip == NULL)
+            return VLC_EGENERIC;
+        *va_arg(args, vlc_tick_t *) = FROM_SCALE(clip->in_time) -
+                                      FROM_SCALE_NZ(clip->start_time);
+        return VLC_SUCCESS;
+    }
+
     case DEMUX_GET_POSITION:
     {
         double *pf_position = va_arg(args, double *);
